---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HistorySources from '../../components/HistorySources.astro';
import entries from '../../data/country-history.json';
import sources from '../../data/history-sources.json';
import coverage from '../../data/history-coverage.json';
---
<BaseLayout title="Country-history inventory" description="Documented commercial-whaling episodes across countries, historical states and maritime networks, with sources, dates and explicit research limits.">
  <header class="container history-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Countries · Historical record</p><h1>A wider history,<br /> one documented episode at a time.</h1><p>This first inventory connects places to evidence of organized commercial whaling. It includes countries, a historical state and a shared maritime network. It is not an exhaustive list or a count of sovereign states.</p><p class="history-date">Research reviewed October 9, 2026 · Coverage review October 24, 2026</p><div class="history-actions"><a href="/historical-economics/">Historical economics →</a><a href="/countries/">Contemporary countries & communities →</a><a href="#coverage">All archive entities &amp; gaps →</a><a href="/countries/history.csv" download>Download these entries (CSV)</a></div></header>
  <section class="container inventory-method" aria-labelledby="reading-inventory"><h2 id="reading-inventory">How to read the inventory</h2><p><strong>Documented episode</strong> means the cited record supports the bounded activity described. It does not certify an entire national history, a current legal position or a motive shared by every participant. Dates describe the example studied, not necessarily the first or last whaling in that place.</p><p>Commercial, Indigenous/subsistence and special-permit research activity remain distinct. Ownership, workforce, operating site and territorial authority are recorded separately where attribution is unresolved. Later policy and legislation require their own dated evidence.</p></section>
  <nav class="container inventory-index" aria-label="Historical places">{entries.map(entry => <a href={`#${entry.id}`}>{entry.name}</a>)}</nav>
  <div class="container inventory-list">{entries.map(entry => <article id={entry.id} class="inventory-entry"><header><p class="eyebrow">{entry.kind}</p><h2>{entry.name}</h2><p>{entry.period}</p></header><div><p class="evidence-label">Documented episode</p><p>{entry.evidence}</p><p><strong>Limits of this entry:</strong> {entry.limits}</p><HistorySources ids={entry.sources as (keyof typeof sources)[]} /></div></article>)}</div>
  <section class="container history-open-questions" id="coverage"><h2>Coverage register: every archive entity.</h2><p>Reviewed October 24, 2026. All 33 archive rows are accounted for below. These are overlapping entities, not a country count. A public episode establishes only its stated scope; a research lead is not promoted to a verified domestic industry.</p><p>Portugal and the Azores map to one public entry. The Soviet Union is not duplicated into successor countries; Basque networks remain a shared history. <a href="/research-status/#coverage">Read the coverage limits</a> and <a href="/research-status/#questions">the full research queue</a>.</p>
    {coverage.map(row => <details class="research-question" id={`coverage-${row.id}`}><summary><span>{row.kind} · {row.status}</span>{row.name}</summary><p><strong>Bounded scope or lead:</strong> {row.scope}</p><p>{row.limits}</p><p>{row.entry ? <a href={`#${row.entry}`}>Read the bounded public episode →</a> : 'No verified domestic-industry entry is asserted here.'}</p><p>Sources: {row.sources.map((id,i) => <>{i > 0 && ' · '}<a href={`/library/history/#${id}`}>{id}</a></>)}</p><p>Open questions: {row.questions.length ? row.questions.map((id,i) => <>{i > 0 && ' · '}<a href={`/research-status/#${id}`}>{id}</a></>) : <a href="/research-status/#Q001">Global attribution and coverage (Q001)</a>}</p></details>)}
    <p>Other places and earlier or smaller enterprises may still be missing. <a href="/contact/">Help extend or correct the record</a> with an identifiable source.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
